      "summary": "The document is an article discussing adverse reactions in two pediatric cases involving the use of Broncholyt. The first case concerns a 6-year-old boy who developed generalized urticaria, facial swelling, and stridor within 30 minutes of taking 5 mL of Broncholyt for a cough. He was treated with intramuscular adrenaline and recovered. The second case involves a 9-year-old girl who experienced vomiting, wheeze, and hypotension two hours after receiving Broncholyt for bronchitis. She required adrenaline treatment and overnight observation but also recovered fully. The document does not include any form fields, tables, or images. It appears relevant to pharmacovigilance as it reports adverse drug reactions in children. Missing information includes the exact dosage for the second case, the specific formulation of Broncholyt, and any prior medical history or potential contributing factors for the reactions.",
